Chapter: SmpDispatch

 Six children are spawned and each spins for a while before exiting. The
 boot processor takes one; every other core is in the same dispatch loop
 and takes one too. Each claim made by a core whose id is not zero adds
 one to cell 36200 with a locked add, and the boot processor's id is
 always zero.

Section: Body

  spin : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  spin (n) (acc) = if n == 0 then acc else spin (n - 1) (acc + 1)

  child-body : Integer -> Integer
  child-body (x) = spin 100000000 0

  opening : [Console, Concurrent] Nothing = act
    a <- process-spawn (\x -> child-body x)
    b <- process-spawn (\x -> child-body x)
    c <- process-spawn (\x -> child-body x)
    d <- process-spawn (\x -> child-body x)
    e <- process-spawn (\x -> child-body x)
    f <- process-spawn (\x -> child-body x)
    wa <- process-wait a
    wb <- process-wait b
    wc <- process-wait c
    wd <- process-wait d
    we <- process-wait e
    wf <- process-wait f
    print-line-uni ("aps checked in: " & show (atomic-load 4080))
    print-line-uni (if atomic-load 36200 > 0
                    then "an ap claimed and ran a process"
                    else "NO AP RAN A PROCESS")
  end
